  "description": "High-performance B+Tree index engine for .NET.\n    Works with MemoryStream or FileStream, fixed-size pages, and deterministic memory use.\n    Suitable for embedded systems, POS terminals, kiosks, scanners, and edge devices.\n    Supports balanced insert/erase, leaf-chain traversal, and deferred flush write-back caching.\n    Ideal for KV stores, embedded storage engines, OLTP index tables, queue logs, and append-only logs.",
  "iconFile": "btree.png",
  "id": "BTreePlus",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2025-11-17T17:04:50.263Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": false,
  "packageHash": "3L/7WOVbhCMgC8kNGKhJtL+wyAvldKJUx3ZnAuBLwglbXSbC9fE+2Z9z2fWuOZJGhbDyLzYV6z0/vsfN/sjsGw==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 80428,
  "published": "1900-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Validated under continuous FileStream workloads with sustained multi-million insert/sec performance on NVMe.\n    - Stable operation confirmed across Windows, Linux, and ARM edge devices.\n    - Page-size rule (1–64, ×512 byte physical sizing) finalized for embedded deployments.\n    - Deferred flush write-back cache proven safe under unexpected power-off scenarios.\n    - Fully suitable for POS terminals, kiosks, scanners, industrial controllers, and transactional OLTP systems.\n    - Commercial support, integration services, and embedded device licensing available.\n    - Added Dicitonary support layer for simplified key-value operations.\n    - Improved concurrency control and lock management for multi-threaded environments.",
